  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Denmark&apos;s Contribution to the 21st Replenishment of the International Development Association (IDA21)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IDA is deepening its support to drive a resilient recovery for the poorest countries through its historic $100 billion 21st replenishment cycle (IDA21) between July 1, 2025 and June 30, 2028. Under the overarching theme of &#x201c;Ending Poverty on a Livable Planet: Delivering Impact with Urgency and Ambition&#x201d;, IDA21 will invest in the future of people and the planet with renewed scale, effectiveness, and financial efficiency. The world&#x2019;s poorest countries have high external financing needs. Multiple crises have set back global development, putting lives and livelihoods at risk and delaying progress toward the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). IDA21 responds to these challenges with an ambitious agenda that will seize opportunities for change. As it supports IDA countries to chart their own paths toward sustainable development, IDA21 will benefit 1.9 billion people around the globe and sustain IDA&#x2019;s record of continuous improvement.</narrative>
  </description>
